real_benzene_nmr_orca5.out and benzene-opt-nmr.out are genuine output files
generated by ORCA (https://orcaforum.kofo.mpg.de/), a quantum chemistry
program developed at the Max Planck Institute for Coal Research.

ORCA is proprietary software distributed free of charge for academic use under
its own license terms. These two files are included here solely as test
fixtures for the parser test suite and are NOT covered by the GPL-3.0 license
that governs the source code of this project.

To regenerate them you need your own ORCA installation and licence.

The other .out files in this directory are synthetic: generated by
make_fixtures.py in ORCA's text layout but with shielding values computed from
an analytic ring-current model, not by ORCA itself. They carry no such
restriction.
